1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,505
Fold this paper forty-two times...

2
00:00:03,505 --> 00:00:05,408
and it would reach the Moon.

3
00:00:05,736 --> 00:00:07,736
But try it yourself, and you'll get stuck

4
00:00:07,736 --> 00:00:08,659
at about seven.

5
00:00:08,929 --> 00:00:10,402
Every fold doubles it.

6
00:00:10,852 --> 00:00:12,314
Ten folds: ten centimetres.

7
00:00:12,584 --> 00:00:14,834
Twenty-three folds: taller than the

8
00:00:14,834 --> 00:00:16,065
tallest building on Earth.

9
00:00:16,335 --> 00:00:18,623
Forty-two? Past the Moon.

10
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:20,078
So why can't you?

11
00:00:20,797 --> 00:00:23,912
Each fold halves the sheet, and every bend

12
00:00:23,912 --> 00:00:25,451
swallows more paper.

13
00:00:25,788 --> 00:00:29,134
In 2002, a student managed twelve folds...

14
00:00:29,134 --> 00:00:30,990
with paper over a kilometre long.

15
00:00:31,298 --> 00:00:32,933
So if you're stuck at seven...

16
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:33,633
it's not you.

17
00:00:33,914 --> 00:00:34,568
It's the paper.
